                            <div class="b-ax"><span>2019</span><span>searches in India</span><span>2026</span></div>
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
                <p class="b-src">Source: Google Trends, India, yearly average of monthly data on one shared scale, pulled 11 Oct 2026. Searches for “82°E” fall to zero after 2024, partly because people stop typing the symbol.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Instagram" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">structure 05, the story on Instagram</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">Kay changes the mood every season. <em>82°E never does.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <div class="b-ig">
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--c:var(--kay);--n:0">
                        <small class="b-lab">@@kaybykatrina</small>
                        <q>It’s Kay to Be You</q>
                        <div class="b-sw" role="img" aria-label="Kay's grid by season: Christmas red, popsicle pink, café coffee, monsoon peach, Kay Skin milk, Diwali sunset.">
                            <span><i style="--s:#A3192C"></i>Christmas</span><span><i style="--s:#E9A3B2"></i>Popsicle</span><span><i style="--s:#8A5A3C"></i>Café blush</span>
                            <span><i style="--s:#EDBFA0"></i>Monsoon</span><span><i style="--s:#F3E1D3"></i>Kay Skin</span><span><i style="--s:#D9572F"></i>Diwali</span>
                        </div>
                        <ul>
                            <li><b>A new colour story</b> for every drop, timed to India’s calendar</li>
                            <li><b>Real brides,</b> every body type, and men wearing the makeup</li>
                            <li><b>Vicky Kaushal</b> as “Chief Approval Officer”: top comment, 2,682 likes</li>
                            <li><b>Katrina</b> in almost every tile</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--c:var(--e82);--n:1">
                        <small class="b-lab">@@82e.official</small>
                        <q>Self-Care Simplified</q>
                        <div class="b-sw" role="img" aria-label="82°E's grid: six recent tiles, minis, lip therapy, body care, cleansing, hydrating and Deepika, all in the same beige.">
                            <span><i style="--s:#D8C2AD"></i>Minis</span><span><i style="--s:#CDB39B"></i>Lip therapy</span><span><i style="--s:#E2D1C0"></i>Body care</span>
                            <span><i style="--s:#C7A88D"></i>Cleansing</span><span><i style="--s:#DBC5B1"></i>Hydrating</span><span><i style="--s:#D3B9A3"></i>Deepika</span>
                        </div>
                        <ul>
                            <li><b>One beige grid,</b> the same hands-on-face pose</li>
                            <li><b>Deepika</b> in about 5 of 24 tiles</li>
                            <li><b>Follows 1 account;</b> “are you closing?” goes unanswered</li>
                            <li><b>Three names:</b> you hear “eighty-two east”, see 82°E, type 82e.official</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="b-lede" style="font-size:clamp(10px,1.1cqw,14px) !important">Anomaly’s account, “All of us are anomalies”, has been silent since 13 Jan 2025. Its own FAQ said it suits straight to wavy hair only, and its “born in India” story was written by a New York company.</p>
                <p class="b-src">Source: the three brands’ Instagram profiles and grids, seen 13 Oct 2026; colours matched by eye to each grid; Anomaly’s story highlights; USPTO (Anomaly marks filed by Maesa, 2019).</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Why 82°E lost" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">the loser, up close</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">82°E’s fame couldn’t fix <em>a name, a price and a blur.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <div class="b-why">
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:0"><em>01</em><b>The name</b><p>A degree sign people can’t type or search, with a meaning that has to be explained</p></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:1"><em>02</em><b>The price</b><p>₹2,700 for 50 ml, about 4.5x Minimalist per ml, and never cut</p></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:2"><em>03</em><b>The branding</b><p>“Self-Care Simplified” never said what it does. Trade press called it “diffused” by 2026.</p></div>
                </div>
                <ul class="b-more">
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:3"><b>Two products</b> at launch, against Kay’s 48</li>
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:4"><b>Late to a shelf:</b> own site for 17 months, Tira only from Apr 2024</li>
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:5"><b>“Clinically proven”</b> meant surveys of about 50 people</li>
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:6"><b>Lost a court case:</b> “Lotus Splash” barred, Feb 2026</li>
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:7"><b>Stopped making:</b> no use-before date points to a batch after spring 2025</li>
                    <li class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:8"><b>Sold out</b> sitewide since mid-2026, with no word to customers</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="b-src">Source: 82e.com, live and via the Wayback Machine (claim banners, use-before dates, stock); launch press kit; Business Today (Nov 2022); LiveLaw (Feb 2026). Use-before dates assume a 24-month shelf life.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Scorecard" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">putting it together</p>
                <h4 class="b-h">Kay checked every box. <em>82°E checked almost none.</em></h4>
                <div class="b-rule"></div>
                <table class="b-score">
                    <thead><tr><th>What it takes</th><th>Kay Beauty</th><th>Anomaly</th><th>82°E</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td>An A-list founder</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>A name you can say and search</td><td class="y">Yes, “Kay”</td><td class="p">Partly, a common word</td><td>No, a degree sign</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>A story people can retell</td><td class="y">Yes, “It’s Kay to Be You”</td><td class="y">Yes, “all of us are anomalies”</td><td>No, a map line</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Price fits the promise</td><td class="y">Yes, mid-priced</td><td class="p">Partly, too cheap in the US, right in India</td><td>No, Kiehl’s prices</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>A partner that also sells it</td><td class="y">Yes, Nykaa</td><td class="p">Partly, Maesa and Target</td><td>No, own site, then Tira late</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Cheap to reach customers</td><td class="y">Yes, 12.5% on marketing</td><td>Never disclosed</td><td>No, 93% in FY24</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>A category where faces sell</td><td class="y">Yes, makeup</td><td>No, haircare</td><td>No, skincare</td></tr>
                        <tr class="out"><td>Result</td><td>₹211.65 cr revenue, ₹21.8 cr profit</td><td>Sold to Reliance, 2026</td><td>₹14.66 cr revenue, ₹12.26 cr loss, sold out by mid-2026</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
                <p class="b-src">Yes, Partly and No are my reading of the evidence on the slides before; every figure is sourced there.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide b-end" data-title="The takeaway" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(bsig)
                <p class="b-kick">the takeaway</p>
                <h4 class="b-title">Fame gets a brand launched. <em>Structure and story decide if it lasts.</em></h4>
                <ul class="b-rules">
                    <li class="b-anim" style="--n:0"><b>Partner with the shelf</b>Co-own the brand with whoever sells it</li>
                    <li class="b-anim" style="--n:1"><b>Price for fans, not fame</b>About twice what fans already pay, never luxury on day one</li>
                    <li class="b-anim" style="--n:2"><b>An easy name, a real story</b>One word anyone can say, one story anyone can retell</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="b-lede b-anim" style="--n:3"><b>The catch:</b> much of what Kay had came from Nykaa, not from Katrina. It sells 85% of its stock to Nykaa and pays Nykaa 8% of every rupee. The lesson for the next A-lister isn’t to be more famous. It’s to choose the right partner.</p>
                <p class="b-lede b-anim" style="--n:4"><b>Epilogue:</b> 82°E made nothing new after about spring 2025 and sold out in mid-2026. In April 2026 Nykaa told the stock exchange it “remains in discussions” about 82°E. The winner’s partner may end up owning the loser.</p>
            </div>
