                <div class="b-plan">
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:0"><b>1. Kay: keep Nykaa as the front door, and Kay Skin at Kay’s price</b><span>Kay Skin sits at 3x everyday brands, against 2x for the makeup. Bring it back into the band. <em>Measure:</em> repeat buyers, not launch sales.</span></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:1"><b>2. 82°E: one shelf, a Goldilocks price</b><span>Relaunch through Nykaa, already in talks, with the moisturiser at ₹899 and ₹299 minis every day. <em>Measure:</em> repeat rate after 90 days.</span></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:2"><b>3. 82°E: give the name a plain-English line</b><span>Say what the brand does on the front of the box, and reply to customers. <em>Measure:</em> branded search volume.</span></div>
                    <div class="b-card b-anim" style="--n:3"><b>4. Anomaly under Reliance: come home for real</b><span>Relaunch on Tira at ₹899 to ₹999, name the real makers instead of “born in India”, and post again. <em>Measure:</em> restock sell-through.</span></div>
                </div>
